## Order of work

Ordered by **cost of delay**, not by value — principle 5c. Something belongs
early when *waiting makes it more expensive*, which is not the same as wanting
it most:

| Kind | Cost of waiting | Goes |
|---|---|---|
| **Debt-accruing** | grows with every cycle you wait | first |
| **Multiplying** | makes every later piece of work cheaper | second |
| **Terminal** | the same whenever you do it | last, by product value |

| Item | State | Why here |
|---|---|---|
| _Replace this row_ | ⬜ | _and say what it costs to defer_ |

